[section:examples Examples]

The `example/` directory contains complete, buildable programs, one per
common use case. The CMake target name matches the file name minus the
extension (`cmake --build build --target rest_crud_server`), and
`cmake --build build --target examples` builds them all. Each file starts
with the `curl` commands that exercise it.

[table Examples shipped with the library
[[Example][What it shows]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/hello_server.cpp hello_server.cpp]]
 [The smallest complete server: two REST routes, a path argument, a query
 argument with a default, and graceful shutdown on `SIGINT`.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/rest_crud_server.cpp rest_crud_server.cpp]]
 [A JSON REST API: CRUD routes over an in-memory store, typed request
 bodies via `boost::describe`, a multipart import of a text file, a domain
 exception mapped to 404 by a soft error handler, and an OpenAPI 3.1
 document generated from the routes.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/htdocs_server.cpp htdocs_server.cpp]]
 [A single-page application behind `handler::htdocs`: hashed assets
 under `/static` cached as immutable with precompressed variants and
 download headers from `on_response`, and the application shell as the
 fallback for client-side routes, on a multi-threaded `io_context`.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/connection_state_server.cpp connection_state_server.cpp]]
 [Per-connection state with `basic_http<conn_state>`: handlers receive
 the connection's object by reference and use it for counting and a quota.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/cookie_session_server.cpp cookie_session_server.cpp]]
 [Cookie-keyed sessions with `context_store` and `with_session`: login,
 logout, `create_if_missing` versus `require`, and idle expiry.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/streaming_server.cpp streaming_server.cpp]]
 [Streaming in both directions: server-sent events from a timer, a JSON
 stream from an `async_generator`, files streamed from disk with spliced
 generators, and uploads consumed through `body_reader` and
 `multipart_reader` without buffering.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/cancellation_server.cpp cancellation_server.cpp]]
 [The cancellation model end to end: an event stream that stops when its
 client disconnects or the server shuts down, a JSON-RPC job that checks
 its `request_scope` and is cancelled by id through `endpoint::cancel`, an
 MCP tool with progress cancelled by `notifications/cancelled`, and a plain
 handler that finishes on `SIGINT` while the streams stop. RAII guards in
 the nested helpers log every interrupted frame.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/proxy_server.cpp proxy_server.cpp]]
 [Asynchronous handlers: a coroutine that fetches an upstream URL with
 Beast and returns the response, plus a timer-based delay route.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/tls_server.cpp tls_server.cpp]]
 [HTTPS with `session::https` and `server::tls`: certificate and key from
 PEM files, handlers registered as for plain HTTP.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/websocket_server.cpp websocket_server.cpp]]
 [Protocol upgrade to WebSocket via `register_raw_handler`, with an echo
 loop.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/jsonrpc_server.cpp jsonrpc_server.cpp]]
 [A JSON-RPC 2.0 calculator: named parameters, batches, notifications, a
 custom error mapper, and per-client state through `with_session`.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/mcp_server.cpp mcp_server.cpp]]
 [An MCP server over Streamable HTTP: tools with generated input schemas,
 resources and URI templates, a prompt, resource subscriptions,
 per-session state, a tool returning typed content with an embedded
 resource, a blob resource, a tool that notifies its own caller through
 `session_info`, a tool that asks the user to confirm through elicitation,
 CORS for browser clients, and Origin validation.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/taskboard_server.cpp taskboard_server.cpp]]
 [One task board exposed over REST (cookie sessions, constrained
 arguments, OpenAPI with a bearer scheme and components), JSON-RPC and
 MCP (annotated tools, templated resources, prompt completion,
 elicitation, logging), plus a per-user event stream under `with_session`,
 CORS, a request-id interceptor, an admin-token interceptor scoped to
 one route that hands a principal to the handler through `attribute_arg`,
 and a multi-threaded `io_context` with graceful shutdown.]]
[[[@https://github.com/rjahanbakhshi/boost.taar/blob/master/example/mcp_stdio_server.cpp mcp_stdio_server.cpp]]
 [The same MCP tools served over stdio, the transport desktop clients
 launch locally.]]
]

Start with `hello_server.cpp`, then the example closest to what you are
building.

[endsect]
